---
description: "Virtuo Services project safety rules. Always follow before making code changes."
alwaysApply: true
---

Before making any code change, read and follow the repository `AGENTS.md`.

This is a live PHP website project. Pushing to main can deploy to production.

Mandatory rules:

- Do not change unrelated files.
- Do not rewrite large parts of the project.
- Do not change `.htaccess`, `server.php`, `router.php`, `sitemap.php`, `error.php`, URLs, redirects, or clean URL behavior unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not install packages.
- Do not run git commit, git push, deploy, database, or destructive commands unless explicitly asked.
- Make the smallest safe change.
- Do not use IAB, in-app browser, Playwright, browser automation, screenshot testing, or end-to-end browser testing unless the user explicitly asks.
- Default validation should be lightweight: `git diff --check` and `php -l` for changed PHP files.
- Show changed files, root cause, validation commands, and remaining browser tests after finishing.
